\f0\fs22 \cf2 Each vehicle contains a separating toilet that divides urine and faeces. In the rear section of the vehicle the collected urine is processed into natural fertiliser in three steps: nitrogen fixation by microorganisms in a bioreactor, removal of hormones and pharmaceutical residues using a charcoal filter and lastly sanitisation. This process is visible to users, highlighting the potential for sustainable nutrient recycling. Once the vehicle\'92s storage is full, the collected and processed urine is autonomously applied to peri-urban fields.}